Compile native code with $CC/$CXX instead of a hardcoded gcc.

Under Bazel the C toolchain is hermetic: clang, its sysroot and its flags come from
//MODULE.bazel's llvm toolchain, and //build:mix_app.bzl passes them to the mix action
as CC/CXX/CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS/LDFLAGS. Bundlex.Toolchain.GCC hardcodes "gcc"/"g++", so every
Membrane native was built by whatever compiler happened to be in the RBE executor image --
unversioned, outside the action key, and silently different from the compiler that builds
the rest of the repo.

Bundlex already ships a toolchain that reads these variables, Bundlex.Toolchain.Custom,
and it is NOT usable here. It is reached only via Bundlex.Platform.get_module(:custom),
which needs get_target!/0 to return :custom, which needs CROSSCOMPILE to be set. That
same variable also feeds Bundlex.get_target/0, and the Membrane plugins derive their
precompiled OS-dep URLs from it: with CROSSCOMPILE=1 every one of them resolves
`{:precompiled, nil}`, falls back to pkg_config and dies with "Package mp3lame was not
found in the pkg-config search path" (likewise opus, vpx, libswresample). Selecting a
different PLATFORM to change the COMPILER moves far more than the compiler.

So the toolchain stays GCC -- platform :linux, precompiled OS deps resolving exactly as
before -- and only the compiler binary and the flags become overridable. Every variable
is optional and falls back to the previous hardcoded value, so this is a no-op outside
Bazel.

--- a/lib/bundlex/toolchain/gcc.ex
+++ b/lib/bundlex/toolchain/gcc.ex
@@ -5,8 +5,6 @@
   alias Bundlex.Native
   alias Bundlex.Toolchain.Common.{Compilers, Unix}
 
-  @compilers %Compilers{c: "gcc", cpp: "g++"}
-
   @impl Toolchain
   def compiler_commands(native) do
     {cflags, lflags} =
@@ -16,7 +14,9 @@
         %Native{} -> {"", ""}
       end
 
-    compiler = @compilers |> Map.get(native.language)
+    compiler = compilers() |> Map.get(native.language)
+    cflags = join_env(cflags, env_flags(native.language))
+    lflags = join_env(lflags, System.get_env("LDFLAGS"))
 
     Unix.compiler_commands(
       native,
@@ -26,4 +26,18 @@
       wrap_deps: &"-Wl,--disable-new-dtags,--whole-archive #{&1} -Wl,--no-whole-archive"
     )
   end
+
+  defp compilers() do
+    %Compilers{
+      c: System.get_env("CC") || "gcc",
+      cpp: System.get_env("CXX") || "g++"
+    }
+  end
+
+  defp env_flags(:c), do: System.get_env("CFLAGS")
+  defp env_flags(:cpp), do: System.get_env("CXXFLAGS")
+
+  defp join_env(flags, nil), do: flags
+  defp join_env(flags, ""), do: flags
+  defp join_env(flags, env), do: "#{flags} #{env}"
 end
